  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Bahamas in embarking on ratification of ILO Conventions Nos. 155 and 187 on occupational safety and health. This initiative was launched by the National Tripartite Council (NTC).

Beneficiaries of these initiatives include all employers and workers. They will benefit from clearer and more effective legal and administrative protections which will be realized through implementing ratified Conventions, including the actions identified at the tripartite consultation workshop and by acting on comments of the ILO supervisory mechanisms. The ILO will work with the NTC and the Ministry of Labour and Public Service.</narrative>
  </description>
